export anchor FilmFestivalStyle:
    number: 90
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Film festival
    idea: The home screen reads like a festival programme on light stock, with laurel wreaths around the week's numbers, a screening schedule grid that runs each project to its premiere, and programme codes on every film.
    base: light
    palette:
        screen: #f6f3ee, the page
        card: #ffffff, the top bar, the schedule and panels
        ink: #161616, text, codes and done bars
        grey: #5d5a55, notes and last week frames
        rule: #dcd6cc, the week grid and hairlines, never text
        film: #e4dfd6, the film strip and time still to go
        redCarpet: #b3202a, the top bar edge, the current nav item and this week frames
        carpetInk: #a01c25, the primary button, red text, overdue and Behind
        laurel: #8a6d1f, wreaths, never text
        green: #276638, On track
        amber: #8c5200, At risk
    type:
        Three stacks. Condensed caps use Avenir Next Condensed, Roboto
        Condensed, Arial Narrow, Helvetica Neue, Arial with font-stretch
        condensed at 800 for the 76px greeting, 52px laurel numbers, 30px
        section titles and 26px brand, and at 700 for 12 to 15px nav,
        buttons and statuses tracked 0.08 to 0.14em. Text uses Futura,
        Century Gothic, Avenir Next, Segoe UI at 16px with 1.5 line height
        and 19px bold film titles. Programme codes use SF Mono, Menlo,
        Consolas at 600 and 12px.
    layout:
        A white top bar with a 4px red lower edge holds a reel mark, the
        condensed caps brand, caps nav with the current item on a red
        block, a boxed search for the programme, the New project button, a
        square bell and the user. The hero is centred like a poster, a red
        caps line Brightwork presents, a huge condensed Good morning, Mara,
        the date in spaced caps and a red ruled line with an exclamation
        disc saying 4 tasks are overdue. The four numbers sit in a row,
        each between two gold laurel branches with the label in tiny caps
        under it. The screening schedule is a table with a black header
        row. Each row has a black code chip such as DES-01, the title, team
        and tasks, then a lane ruled by weeks from 31 Oct to 15 Jan where a
        bar runs from today to the due date labelled Premiere, filled in
        black to the percentage, with the status under it. The schedule
        scrolls sideways inside its box on narrow screens. Below, a
        festival bulletin lists activity with red mono times, and the reel
        shows the chart as a film strip with sprocket holes and one frame
        per day. Below 960px the bulletin and reel stack and laurels go two
        by two.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 56px between programme sections and 14px inside schedule rows.
    density: Medium. A big poster top, then a tight schedule grid.
    corners: Square everywhere, like printed programme boxes.
    borders: 2px ink on controls and schedule bars, a 4px red edge under the top bar and 1px rules in the grid.
    shadows: None. Flat print.
    icons:
        Gold laurel wreaths and a reel mark. On track is a star, At risk a
        triangle, Behind a square and overdue an exclamation disc, all with
        condensed caps words.
    focus: A 3px ink outline offset 2px, then a screen coloured gap and a 2px red ring out to 9px.
    tone: A festival announcer, such as Brightwork presents, Premiere 14 Nov, Screening schedule and The reel.
